  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e829e438-81b1-5302-8979-6efe832b5c21",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x-4y &=9 \\\\ 4x+6y &=8 \\\\ 10x+2y &=39\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent dependent\n- **II.** The system is inconsistent\n- **III.** The system has a unique solution",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 39\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 4 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 39\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 26 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 39\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 26 \\\\ 0 & -18 & 84\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-9){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}-2 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 26 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -150\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y=-150,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement II is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bdb2acb6-99fc-5500-bd29-cbe20bfb1dfa",
