  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186115299,
      "id": "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac",
      "title": "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "523afc2c-a851-5ee1-a2a7-3f7bd8e19862",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-8y+3z &=-2 \\\\ -2x-6y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system has no solution\n- **II.** The system is consistent independent\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 0 & 10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}4 & -8 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -10 & \\frac{3}{2} & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means that  we can find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*. \n\nAs a result, only statement III is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "42d80745-5de3-51fe-8023-d67341d27dc8",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
