    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1a75f68b-6fec-5130-9d49-0706a1881af0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y &=5 \\\\ 6x+14y &=21 \\\\ -4x-8y &=-10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is consistent independent\n- **II.** The system has no solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 14 & 21 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -10\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 14 & 21 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -10\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y &=5 \\\\ 2y &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=3$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=-\\frac{7}{2}.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
