    "question": {
      ":question/id": "32f0fd56-61f9-5bd3-a15a-623ca58f3d24",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-2z &=2 \\\\ -3x+6y+6z &=13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The system is inconsistent\n- **II.** The system has a unique solution\n- **III.** The system is consistent dependent",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 6 & 13\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 6 & 6 & 13\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 19\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=19,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "66a74cfb-7eef-5393-b361-80a542707807",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
